  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Indonesian Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially resigned from his position. The formal submission of his resignation letter to the People's Consultative Assembly and President Prabowo Subianto concluded a period of intense political activity. Prior to the resignation, members of eight factions within the House of Representatives had signed a motion expressing their intent to pursue impeachment against the Vice President. While some political groups characterize the resignation as a demonstration of statesmanship, others have interpreted the move as a tactical maneuver intended to preempt formal impeachment proceedings. Following the announcement, reports confirmed that the Vice President has vacated the Vice Presidential Palace. The transition has had notable financial implications, with economic monitors observing significant volatility in currency markets as the rupiah reached a new record low.",
